WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.905 --> 00:00:09.086
Plain text goes to the leader of the project at hand.

2
00:00:09.086 --> 00:00:15.554
It reads the checkout, splits your request into cards and posts them on the board;

3
00:00:15.554 --> 00:00:17.290
the workers take them.

4
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:21.076
Its reply comes back as an item waiting for you.

5
00:00:22.294 --> 00:00:24.720
At-name writes to one agent.

6
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.787
After the at sign, tab completes the names, the project at hand first.

7
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:36.246
A message to an idle worker opens a card; its answer closes it.

8
00:00:36.246 --> 00:00:43.092
A line that starts with a slash is the agent's own command line: slash compact,

9
00:00:43.092 --> 00:00:46.905
slash cost, whatever the vendor's CLI knows.

10
00:00:48.106 --> 00:00:53.395
v opens your conversation with the agent at hand, here the leader.

11
00:00:53.395 --> 00:00:59.485
Every message on the bus has a number, and a reply names the one it answers.

12
00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:05.816
Enter on a line of the journal opens the conversation it belongs to; a reply is

13
00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:11.826
marked with an arrow, and the percent key goes to what it answers and back.

14
00:01:11.826 --> 00:01:18.557
The brackets go from turn to turn: the lines one side says before the other answers.

15
00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:32.238
Hash and a number, or hash and a word of its title, opens a card's screen: who works

16
00:01:32.238 --> 00:01:37.316
on it, its story, the inbox and journal lines about it.

17
00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:41.654
n and p step to the next and the previous card.

18
00:01:45.497 --> 00:01:49.655
Every key that acts has a colon name too.

19
00:01:49.655 --> 00:01:58.073
Colon and tab show the commands with what each stands at now: the theme, the budget

20
00:01:58.073 --> 00:02:03.246
spent and left, the project a bare command acts on.

21
00:02:03.246 --> 00:02:08.722
A dollar sign marks the ones that raise the next bill.

22
00:02:08.722 --> 00:02:13.388
Colon budget changes the pot while agents run.

23
00:02:14.589 --> 00:02:20.966
Colon theme wears each theme while its name is written: the built-in ones, base16

24
00:02:20.966 --> 00:02:25.453
schemes, or a colour file in Ghostty's or Kitty's format.

25
00:02:25.453 --> 00:02:28.209
Enter keeps it, escape gives it up.

26
00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:33.720
The terminal theme follows your terminal's own colours, light or dark.

27
00:02:34.922 --> 00:02:38.919
Capital L turns the screen Turkish, and back.

28
00:02:38.919 --> 00:02:46.026
Every word on the screen lives in both languages; what an agent wrote is cleaned

29
00:02:46.026 --> 00:02:53.133
before it is drawn, control characters removed and secret-looking tokens hidden.

30
00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:58.227
Question mark lists every key and every command.

31
00:02:58.227 --> 00:03:04.878
Slash filters them by every word you type, Turkish letters or not; enter keeps the

32
00:03:04.878 --> 00:03:06.825
filter, escape drops it.

33
00:03:09.559 --> 00:03:17.998
f shows only what needs you: waiting for you, stuck, done and not yet seen, in that

34
00:03:17.998 --> 00:03:20.946
order; calm agents fold away.

35
00:03:20.946 --> 00:03:29.081
h and l fold and unfold a project; a folded project is one line that still shows

36
00:03:29.081 --> 00:03:30.199
what waits.

37
00:03:30.199 --> 00:03:38.130
Colon open adds another checkout as a project of its own, with its own leader.

38
00:03:39.331 --> 00:03:43.822
One line to the leader, and a key for everything else.

